  "redone": "Title: On marginalia\nDate: 2026-11-07\nAuthor: A. Writer\nTags: format, samples\n\nMarginalia are what a reader leaves beside the text: **bold words**, *italic ones*, `inline code`, [a link](https://example.com/marginalia), another document, [a heading here](<#Lists>), and a citation[^1] \\[knuth84\\]. Café, naïve, 日本語.\n\n## Lists\n\n- A bullet\n\n  - A nested bullet\n\n- First\n\n1. Second\n\n> A quotation, set in italics.\n\n### Pictures and code\n\n[![](images/figure.png)](https://example.com/figure)\n\n![](../pictures/photo.jpg)\n\n---\n\n```rust\nfn main() {\n    println!(\"marginalia\");\n}\n```\n\n```\nplain   code,\n  exactly\n```\n\n> Verse keeps its lines,\\\n>     and its spacing,\\\n> exactly.\n\nThe end, with a footnote[^2], and a closing word. Merged in. An afterthought.\n\n[^1]: The first footnote, citing \\[knuth84\\].\n[^2]: The second footnote.\n",
